+| `23-web-page` | Does a browser keep a `__Host-` cookie from a self-signed IP-literal host after a click-through, does `connect-src 'self'` admit `wss:`, and what do five parallel connections meet? | A throwaway HTTPS server with the five browser steps written down; not driven on the Mac. The owner's iPad, iPhone and Android tablet kept the cookie and paired through the page (2026-10-23). Against the app's pool, five connections at once: four answered, the fifth closed at accept every round, so the page reads its projects' sessions one at a time on its kept connection. |
 | `04-terminal-view` | Embedded terminal or hand-off? | Hand off agents to Ghostty (`open -na Ghostty --args ... -e cmd`, raise by title); embed `egui_term` for shells, commands, services. |
 
